{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent.\n\n- **Launch command:** the `command` property is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim.\n  - A missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default.\n  - Reason: the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists.\n- **Role:** `role` says what the agent is for.\n  - `prop:role=reviewer` lists the review bench.\n  - `prop:role=author` lists who can hold a lane.\n- **Split:** the note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts.\n- **Spawn shape:** `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`\n- When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window (`opus[1m]`), YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default. The `[1m]` suffix is the human's ruling of 2026-08-21 — a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia.","changed":"2026-08-21T21:52:55-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix, ruled by the human 2026-08-21 (on the Anthropic API Opus 5 is 1M natively; the suffix pins it everywhere and is harmless where it is the default)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode.\n\n- Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree.\n- Posts one review comment via gh.\n- Never edits, pushes, or merges.\n- **Authoring track record:**\n  - Shipped #64 (home-manager module) and #153 (parallel e2e) as author.\n  - 2026-08-16: its quiet-outline UI authoring attempt was judged bad by the human and discarded wholesale (terminal killed, no commits worth keeping).\n  - **Guidance:** prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy authoring, grok for reviews and infra-shaped authoring.","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2","title":"opencode — reviewer","desc":"opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here).\n\n- Same reviewer contract as grok.\n- **Quirks:**\n  - Has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name.\n  - On PR #193 (2026-08-15) its review asserted \"nothing else in docs//website/ enumerates chat rows or _meta fields, so no drift\" — wrong on both counts (grok found both).\n  - Weigh its no-drift claims accordingly.","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. Added 2026-08-19 on the human's word, for design-first work (first use: the vault-in-browser design doc).\n- Reserve for work needing that level — it is the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author.\n- Verify with the banner: it must say Fable, not the machine default.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"supervision-watcher","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a4","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"The wake mechanism (per instructions.md): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore-self --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21).\n\nThe mute list, as `--ignore` flags — fail-open (a stale id costs nothing; every NEW terminal still rings), which is what keeps it legal under the never-an-id-list doctrine. Muted 2026-08-21, all explicitly dispositioned as the HUMAN's own sessions: 0cdc41be + a5e17829 + ab047416 (the kolu#2194 handover — the human took that lane over with their own Claude; orchestrator stands down until handed back), aa15d349 (kolu·damn-spring), 3d01a0b3 (merged docs-PR session), 7251ff2b (nixos-config), 1ef72cfc (olai·master chat session), 2080355a. A terminal handed back to the orchestrator is unmuted by re-arming without its flag; a new human session that starts nagging gets muted the same way after its disposition is verified — never on assumption (identify via kolu ls first).\n\nNag discipline (RCA-2, 2026-08-21): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — the second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate it as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.","created":"2026-08-21T17:30:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T01:11:06-04:00","custom":{"deploy-2026-08-21":"DEPLOYED ~21:20 and then the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn); the SECOND restart recycled all terminal ids (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten. Production kolu now carries #2194; full real-agent verification run 21:28 (test terminal c01109d6).","mute-list":"as of 2026-08-22 01:13 (re-armed): --ignore-self + ce01171b (the human's grok in nixos-config) + 6fc30332 (the one-search-box author, PARKED on the human's word: PR #334 fielded, pipeline complete, terminal kept alive to address the human's morning findings — unmuted by re-arming without its flag when the human hands it back). Fail-open; new terminals still ring.","odu-venue":"2026-08-21 20:50, the human's word — the CI pool is contended: agents run odu CI on LOCALHOST (`nix run github:juspay/odu -- run --platform x86_64-linux --host x86_64-linux=localhost`), strict and posting as always; goes in every future brief. Caveat the orchestrator watches: concurrent localhost e2e runs from several worktrees now share THIS machine's cores — stagger dispatches if runs collide. #327's kolu-ci-1 experiment exempt (pinned by design).","verification-2026-08-21":"production kolu#2194 FULL TEST with a real agent (c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY 42 in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition at +10s arriving instantly (per-line flush VERIFIED); nag re-ring at exactly +45s and +90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design (no gone event, per the contract). Orchestrator's verdict on #2194: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build; merge-ready from the consumer's seat.","watch-task":"bn8bcjm4z (re-armed 2026-08-22 01:13 with --ignore 6fc30332 added; b243brm8x stopped deliberately, not dead)"}}
